#: ../../source/readme_rosetta.rst:16
msgid "readme_rosetta.lang_codes module"
msgstr ""
"`Readme`\n"
"================\n"
"\n"
"**Rosetta**\n"
"---------\n"
"\n"
"`lang_codes.py`\n"
"\n"
"### Lang Codes\n"
"\n"
"*   `.ISO 639-3`: International Organization for Standardization (ISO) code for language\n"
"*   `.ISO 4217`: International Organization for Standardization (ISO) code for currency\n"
"*   `.`: Default language code when no code is specified\n"
"*   `_` : Language code with underscore\n"
"\n"
"### Available Codes\n"
"\n"
"| Lang Code | Description |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"|.iso-639-3| ISO 639-3 standard for languages|\n"
"| .iso-4217| ISO 4217 standard for currencies|\n"
"| `.default`| Default language code when no code is specified|\n"
"\n"
"**Lang Codes**\n"
"---------------\n"
"\n"
"*   **.ISO 639-3**: [International Organization for Standardization (ISO) code for language](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_639-2)\n"
"*   **.ISO 4217**: [International Organization for Standardization (ISO) code for currency](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_4217)\n"
"\n"
"**Available Codes**\n"
"------------------\n"
"\n"
"| Lang Code | Description |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"|.iso-639-3| [Language code standard](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Language_code_(ISO_639))|\n"
"| .iso-4217| [Currency code standard](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Currency_code_(ISO_4217))|\n"
"\n"
"Note: Please refer to the official ISO standards for more information."

#: of readme_rosetta.lang_codes:1
msgid "Mapping of ISO language codes to their full English names."
msgstr ""
"**ISO 639-1 Codes**\n"
"\n"
"* **en** - English\n"
"* **da** - Danish\n"
"* **fr** - French\n"
"* **de** - German\n"
"* **es** - Spanish\n"
"* **it** - Italian\n"
"* **pt** - Portuguese\n"
"* **nl** - Dutch\n"
"* **ru** - Russian\n"
"* **ar** - Arabic\n"
"* **he** - Hebrew\n"
"* **hi** - Hindi\n"
"* **ja** - Japanese\n"
"* **ko** - Korean\n"
"* **cn** - Chinese (Simplified)\n"
"* **tw** - Chinese (Traditional)\n"
"\n"
"**ISO 639-2 Codes**\n"
"\n"
"* **en** - English (B, T)\n"
"* **da** - Danish (Dan)\n"
"* **fr** - French (Fra)\n"
"* **de** - German (Deu)\n"
"* **es** - Spanish (Esp)\n"
"* **it** - Italian (Ita)\n"
"* **pt** - Portuguese (Por)\n"
"* **nl** - Dutch (Ned)\n"
"* **ru** - Russian (RUS)\n"
"* **ar** - Arabic (Arb)\n"
"* **he** - Hebrew (Heb)\n"
"* **hi** - Hindi ( Hin)\n"
"* **ja** - Japanese (Jpn)\n"
"* **ko** - Korean (Kor)\n"
"* **cn** - Chinese (Simp)\n"
"* **tw** - Chinese (Trad)"

#: ../../source/readme_rosetta.rst:24
msgid "readme_rosetta.markdown_handler module"
msgstr ""
"```markdown\n"
"README.md handler for Rosetta\n"
"\n"
"Rosetta is a machine translation service provided by Microsoft. The `readme_rosetta.markdown_handler` module provides a handler for Markdown files, which allows for formatting and highlighting of Markdown text.\n"
"\n"
"This handler supports the following features:\n"
"\n"
"*   Headers (1-6 levels)\n"
"*   Bold text\n"
"*   Italic text\n"
"*   Strikethrough text\n"
"*   Links\n"
"*   Images\n"
"\n"
"It also supports code blocks, which can be used to highlight source code or other types of text.\n"
"\n"
"You can use this handler in your Rosetta project by importing the `readme_rosetta.markdown_handler` module and using its methods to format and render Markdown text.\n"
"```"

